            <ArticleTitle>[A method of determining the phospholipase activity of erythrocytes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A method for measuring the activity of the red cell endogenous phospholipase A is suggested, consisting in red cell destruction, extraction of erythrocytic phospholipase, and detection of the enzymic activity by phosphatidylcholine hydrolysis in the organic phase from the degree of clarification of the lecithin emulsion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
